#!/usr/bin/env bash
# Run the cheap half of the preflight before every push.
#
# scripts/preflight-push.sh only helps if somebody remembers to run it, and the
# push that added it went red on CI precisely because I pushed without it. A
# check that depends on discipline is not a check.
#
# --fast is deliberate: it takes ~19 seconds and covers every failure class that
# actually went red this session - lockfile drift, a lint error, a syntax error,
# an inline script that does not parse, a script that needs a CLI CI does not
# have, a rewrite pointing at a deleted page, a 13th Serverless Function. It
# SKIPS the 8-minute browser suite, so this is a fast gate rather than a full
# one; run `scripts/preflight-push.sh` (no flag) for that before anything that
# matters.
#
# Escape hatch: `git push --no-verify` skips this entirely. It is here so a
# broken hook can never stop you pushing - not as the normal path.
cd "$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)" || exit 0
[ -f scripts/preflight-push.sh ] || exit 0

if ! bash scripts/preflight-push.sh --fast; then
  cat >&2 <<'MSG'

PUSH BLOCKED by .githooks/pre-push (the fast preflight failed above).

Fix the reported problem, or push anyway with:
  git push --no-verify
MSG
  exit 1
fi
